# Everything listed here is left OUT of the "build context" -- the copy of
# this folder that `docker build` ships to the Docker engine before the build
# starts. Without this file the context is 89.3 MB / 1,602 files; with it,
# about 14 MB. Smaller context = faster builds and a smaller image.
#
# Anything excluded here simply does not exist as far as the Dockerfile is
# concerned: a COPY cannot reach it.
#
# NOTE THE `**/` PREFIXES, they are load-bearing. A pattern with no slash in it
# is matched against the path relative to the context ROOT only -- so a bare
# `*.compiled.pkl` excludes a pickle sitting next to this file and does NOTHING
# about workbook/*.compiled.pkl. That is not hypothetical: the first build of
# this image shipped the 40 MB Windows-built pickle and Excel's lock file into
# workbook/ for exactly that reason, and the RUN step that was supposed to
# rebuild the pickle instead found a valid cache and loaded it in 0.9 s. It was
# only caught by listing the directory inside the image. `**/` matches at any
# depth, which is what these patterns meant all along.

# ── Version history ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 25.7 MB of git objects. The image runs code; it has no use for history.
.git/
.gitignore

# ── Python bytecode ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compiled on Windows. The container is Linux; let it compile its own.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# ── The compiled workbook pickle (39.4 MB) ───────────────────────────────
# THE important exclusion. workbook_model.py caches the parsed workbook as a
# pickle, and a pickle is bound to the interpreter and class definitions that
# wrote it -- this one came from Windows Python 3.14.6. The Dockerfile
# regenerates it inside the image with the image's own Python, so the file is
# correct by construction instead of correct by luck. A stale pickle that
# happens to load is a worse failure than one that refuses to.
**/*.compiled.pkl

# ── Excel's lock artifact ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A ~165 B file Excel writes while the workbook is open. Currently present
# at workbook/~$IESS2047_Version_3.0.xlsx, i.e. NOT at the context root.
**/~$*.xlsx

# ── Not needed at runtime ────────────────────────────────────────────────
tests/                              # 8.2 MB of golden fixtures
img/                                # 0.5 MB; Flask serves ui/static, not this
CLAUDE_CODE_PROJECT_CONTEXT.md      # 524 KB of project notes
fullcomparision.md
jolinsonrichie-*.json               # 324 KB export, unused by the app
ui/debug_supply_chart.png

# ── Docker's own files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No reason to copy these into the image they describe.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml

# ── NOT excluded, deliberately ───────────────────────────────────────────
#   cache/            4.4 MB, 1,227 files -- the pre-computed pathway cache.
#                     This is the warm start: it covers all 4 presets and
#                     every single-lever tweak from each, so those are
#                     instant cache hits that never touch the engine. Its
#                     keys are sha256(xlsx) + output-schema hash + lever
#                     vector, all platform-independent, so a cache built on
#                     Windows is valid inside a Linux container.
#   workbook/*.xlsx   8.9 MB -- the model itself. Obviously required.
